/// #2065 wall 1 (ADR-0076 追記34): a FIRST-ORDER row-variable callee reached
/// under an injected Async entry boundary.
///
/// The ADR-0076 追記34 V1 guard refuses only when three independent
/// conditions hold at once. This fixture holds all three:
///   (1) an Async entry boundary is injected -- `sleep` under an
///       `allows Async` entry (lc_inject_async_sleep_boundary);
///   (2) a row-variable callee, whose row `edp_row_labels_have_var` sees;
///   (3) a top-level fn with an Async-row function-typed parameter, which
///       `edp_any_row_typed_param` finds with NO reachability test -- the
///       unused `takes_async_fn` declaration below is enough on its own.
///
/// Before `edp_callee_first_order`, condition (2) withheld `via` from
/// `pure_fns` unconditionally, the migration failed to plan, and the whole
/// program was refused with the "type-directed evidence" hard error.
///
/// `via` takes one annotated, non-function parameter and returns a bare type
/// parameter, so no argument can carry a row and its variable `e` can only
/// be instantiated to the EMPTY row. The call cannot perform `Async`, the
/// migration plans, and the program answers 42.
///
/// The higher-order twin that must STAY refused is
/// fixtures/err_async_rowvar_higher_order_refused.vibe.
fn takes_async_fn[T](f: () -> T with Async) -> Int {
  0
}

fn via[T, e](x: T) -> T with e {
  x
}

fn main() -> Int allows Async {
  sleep(1)
  via(42)
}
